# The eval harness pipes the agent's reply into handoff.txt inside this working
# copy, and a --verify-tree gate rightly refuses to commit around an undeclared
# file. Ignored files do not appear in `git status --porcelain`, so this keeps
# the harness's own artifact out of every lane's tree check.
handoff.txt
node_modules/

# The batch lane creates one git worktree per bug. A worktree placed INSIDE this
# working copy would otherwise show up as an untracked directory in the main
# tree's `git status`, which is noise the graders and the gates do not need.
# Ignored here rather than forbidden in the prompt: where the worktrees live is
# the lane's decision, not the case's.
wt/
worktrees/
.worktrees/
